                <pb facs="0796" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg786"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3131/127: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Nicholson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-19T18:00:00-04:30">October 19, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Department’s telegram No. 56, October 7, 7 p.m. and my telegram No. 98,
                    October 15, 6 p.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d769-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Venezuelan Government is now ready to have the preliminary announcement made
                    simultaneously in Washington and Caracas. Please inform me by telegraph when
                    announcement will be made. The Foreign Minister prefers that no lists be
                    published pending the informal exchange referred to in the second paragraph of
                    my telegram No. 98.</p>
                <p>A copy of the Foreign Minister’s note of today’s date agreeing to announcement
                    and enclosing his amended draft general provisions is being forwarded by air
                    mail today with my despatch No. 847.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d769-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nicholson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
